{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Context for this doc change (machine-local, not part of the repo diff): on the operator's\nhost Serena has been re-pointed from the working checkout to a dedicated read-only clone of\n`origin/main`, refreshed hourly by a `StartInterval=3600` LaunchAgent modelled on the\nexisting `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`. The updater unlocks the tree, fetches, and relocks\nfrom an EXIT trap, so a failed or interrupted update cannot leave it writable.\n\nVerified before writing this ticket's change: a Serena read against the mirror returns\nsymbols; a Serena `replace_content` write against it fails with `PermissionError` and leaves\nthe mirror `git status` clean; the operator checkout is untouched.\n\nThat host detail is deliberately OUT of the repo change — `AGENTS.md` gets only the\nhost-agnostic facts (read-only mirror of `origin/main`, refreshed on a lag) so the guidance\nholds for any environment configured this way."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787951230047193415,"uuid":"74e4a749-4f1e-4496-89a3-b4b1badae255"}